{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/601016-on-demon-the-fallen-and-the-umbra","id":601016,"title":"On Demon: the Fallen and the Umbra","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-23T16:03:20-07:00","id":601016,"title":"On Demon: the Fallen and the Umbra","content":"Has any explanation (or for that matter, consideration) been given to The Fallen and their relationship (or lack thereof) with the Umbra?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T17:09:45-07:00","id":601069,"title":"","content":"Honestly I don't know. From what I gathered there's only three realms Demons recognize, reality, Heaven, and Hell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T04:47:17-07:00","id":601602,"title":"","content":"They do relate to the Umbra and can travel there with the right Lore. By the way, they know of and can travel to almost all reallities described in any cWoD book, just are out-of-date with such information right after leaving Hell.<br /> <br /> By the way, they CREATED some realities, including the entire Dark Umbra. Charon is a Demon, by the way (don't know how he escaped the pit).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T06:31:55-07:00","id":601724,"title":"","content":"The other Umbras are never-ever-mentioned in Demon. And, unless you use a more &quot;dynamic&quot; approach to Lore, or create a ritual or an artifact, they're unreachable.<br /> <br /> In fact, they're non existent. As a proof, note that Demon version of Werewolves travel to the Dark Umbra when they step sideways. And if werewolves doesn't travel to Middle Umbra, then who?<br /> <br /> In the end, it all depends on if you want the other Umbras to be a thing in your game or not. Demon doesn't support them (no written rules), but it isn't difficult to imagine ways to reach them, where they to exist. Using rituals or artifacts you may craft a way to get there (probably involving the Lore of the Realms, along with any other Lore that the Storyteller deems appropriate)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T08:25:24-07:00","id":601840,"title":"","content":"The Earthbound sourcebook has rules for those characters to interact with/draw upon the Middle Umbral realms, but they're presented as a more recent development that they've gained knowledge of thanks to their millennia of habitation on the Earth rather than something demons were familiar with from way back when.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T08:38:56-07:00","id":601868,"title":"","content":"It's been posited the many other times this subject has come up as a thread or ended up being part of another thread, that it is very likely that the Demon line hadn't gotten around to dealing with the Middle Umbra yet before it got the knife across the throat with the rest of the CWOD. There are some placeholder ideas, like Werewolves going to the Dark Umbra (which is about as unlike Apocalypse Werewolves as Vampire Lupines... in other worlds &quot;totally in line with many similar WoDs&quot; view of hyper-reality). There are also some indicators that it was something that would be dealt with later in more detail, such as Earthbound as Matt pointed out (and if any demons should know about the Middle Umbra, it would be Earthbound, being as they have been on Earth for centuries.)<br /> <br /> DtF definitely indicated that the demons were from a time when the Umbra and the &quot;Real World&quot; were completely integrated One of the conciets of the game appears to be that demons feel the world has changed so much for the worst because all of the &quot;depth&quot; has been erased. When pressed for what they mean, what they seem to mean is the aspects of reality that have &quot;broken&quot; off and become the Umbra. It's a sort of &quot;mind blindness&quot;. Their perceptions are too focused on the &quot;material&quot; world.<br /> <br /> If they became aware of the Middle Umbra, you might see a whole faction arise that would be trying to re-integrate the two worlds, probably with disastrous consequence for both, but, oh well, to those demons it would be &quot;better&quot; because that's the way &quot;things are supposed to be&quot;. Everything would just have to deal with it, &quot;for their own good.&quot; <br /> <br /> Also, the demons are equally blind to the mages' High Umbra as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T09:05:26-07:00","id":601901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Earthbound sourcebook has rules for those characters to interact with/draw upon the Middle Umbral realms, but they're presented as a more recent development that they've gained knowledge of thanks to their millennia of habitation on the Earth rather than something demons were familiar with from way back when.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you mention them?. Because if you refer to the Lore that allows to invoke Chaos, how do you know that they're talking about the Middle Umbra, and not the Deep Umbra ?, or any other &quot;chaotic&quot; layer/realm ?. Or even some entirely different dimension known only by the Earthbounds ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T17:06:43-07:00","id":602370,"title":"","content":"Demons can travel to the Shadowlands. The Shadowlands are the first level of umbra before reaching the underworld, and places like Haven (which Demons built and can go to).<br /> <br /> The Shadowlands are connected to the Umbra that Werewolves travel to, and werewolves can get to them as well.<br /> <br /> All of this stuff is just a spectrum of hypercubes, realities upon realities. I think werewolf umbra and dead people umbra are mostly in the same place, just shifted a few degrees apart. Or, they're the same place and people's experiences are drastically altered in part by their expectations. Their perceptions determine the reality they're in.<br /> <br /> Source books will often vary pretty heavily when describing the physics (or metaphysics) of the WoD in a way that skews it for the more beneficial telling of that splat's story. These don't always mesh together seamlessly, because there is so much going on. The world is being described to you differently because of the outlooks of those books. I'd suggest that some parts of the world are literally different (to an extent) based on who's looking at it in the WoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6883-darkexcalibur42","name":"DarkExcalibur42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6883_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T17:07:38-07:00","id":602371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/601016-on-demon-the-fallen-and-the-umbra?p=601901#post601901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can you mention them?. Because if you refer to the Lore that allows to invoke Chaos, how do you know that they're talking about the Middle Umbra, and not the Deep Umbra ?, or any other &quot;chaotic&quot; layer/realm ?. Or even some entirely different dimension known only by the Earthbounds ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Chaos isn't the middle umbra. it MIGHT be the deep umbra, but more likely it's actually stuff outside our universe being let in. Things from the primordial chaos which the creator crafted the world from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6883-darkexcalibur42","name":"DarkExcalibur42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6883_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T19:10:46-07:00","id":602427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkExcalibur42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/601016-on-demon-the-fallen-and-the-umbra?p=602370#post602370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demons can travel to the Shadowlands. The Shadowlands are the first level of umbra before reaching the underworld, and places like Haven (which Demons built and can go to).<br /> <br /> The Shadowlands are connected to the Umbra that Werewolves travel to, and werewolves can get to them as well.<br /> <br /> All of this stuff is just a spectrum of hypercubes, realities upon realities. I think werewolf umbra and dead people umbra are mostly in the same place, just shifted a few degrees apart. Or, they're the same place and people's experiences are drastically altered in part by their expectations. Their perceptions determine the reality they're in.<br /> <br /> Source books will often vary pretty heavily when describing the physics (or metaphysics) of the WoD in a way that skews it for the more beneficial telling of that splat's story. These don't always mesh together seamlessly, because there is so much going on. The world is being described to you differently because of the outlooks of those books. I'd suggest that some parts of the world are literally different (to an extent) based on who's looking at it in the WoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>NB: The Dark Umbra is composed of a completely different spiritual substance (plasm; the Middle Umbra is composed of ephemera). Ghosts can't shape ephemera with Moliate like they can with plasm. Most of the features of the Middle Umbra are also absent, to the point where no one can really find them. Crossing the two is a taxing journey, with the only straightforward passageway being a trip through the Thousand Hells.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T23:10:31-07:00","id":610454,"title":"","content":"My general way of looking at it is that the Demons simply aren't accustomed to having a *completely separate place for spirits*.<br /> <br /> In their heyday, Reality was unified. Every person, place and thing functioned on a material and spiritual level. There was no need to distinguish between &quot;Reality&quot; and &quot;Umbra&quot; because it was all one and the same. The humans that existed believed only in God and the Angels, there was no Gauntlet or Paradox. Matter that decayed and animals that perished didn't *go* anywhere, they were simply recycled directly into new energy. There was only Creation and *not Creation*, AKA the Abyss.<br /> <br /> Now the Demons emerge and find the Engines have broken down. Creation is no longer unified, somewhere along the way the Gauntlet went up, separating Spirit and Matter, and the humans forgot what God truly is, focusing entirely on themselves and their own needs rather than something greater.<br /> <br /> So they don't have any experience with the Umbra. The Slayers have experience with the Shadow Realms, of course, and the Malefactors have pocket realms hidden all over the Universe, but not on the same scale as the Umbra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7113-machiavalium","name":"Machiavalium","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T10:42:21-07:00","id":611057,"title":"","content":"It would be interesting to see how the Demons would reacting in the Wyrm-related realms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T12:21:01-07:00","id":611170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yaoi Huntress Earth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/601016-on-demon-the-fallen-and-the-umbra?p=611057#post611057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would be interesting to see how the Demons would reacting in the Wyrm-related realms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Soaking up Torment like crazy when not trying to flee from clouds of banes intent on devouring the delicious candy that is their Faith pool, most likely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T18:31:10-07:00","id":622979,"title":"","content":"they can get to the lands of the dead but officially they have no way to get to other parts of the umbra, I use a houserule that gives them a 10% chance to enter a random umbral realm, once they know there are multiple realms though they will be able to use paths or what not to go their themselves","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T13:17:28-07:00","id":658305,"title":"","content":"In Houses of the Fallen it is described how, with Paradise already broken (Paradise being the whole realities unified), Slayers and Reapers fought each other throughout other realities before the creation of the Shadowlands. This ability (one maybe or maybe not shared with other Fallen) let the Halaku build a fortress at the center of the Earth and ultimately design the Lands of the Dead which they view as their new Heaven.<br /> <br /> It can be asumed that, as spirits (and spirits that forged cosmos), the Angels and the Fallen were able to travel to these pieces of the shatered reality (much like Garou can). Nonethless the Umbra they knew then was one more pure, recently separated pieces of the world, like the peel of a fruit discarded aside, sharing with material world a weak realtion but in no sense other worlds on themselves. <br /> <br /> The modern Umbrae (for cWoD) has in some way crafted itself from this layers just as the Slayers created a Heaven for their allies. The emotions, dreams, hopes and fears of the denizens of the world found their way to the forgoten skin that once was a piece of Paradise, forming the spirit realms which in time would become to be conected at varios points of their vast geography.<br /> <br /> So the Fallen will no longer recognize this layers of reality if they see it: rind rotten, infested and festering with a new kind of existence that never was really intended to exist (or maybe it was. Long before the Fall, Usiel noted that the cosmos was changing without angelic intervention). Besides their power is diminished for the Fall and Hell and they are riding mortal flesh, so it is unlikely that they can interact or even percive Umbra. At least soon after the walls of Hell let them scape from their prision. <br /> <br /> Indeed the discovery of the ephemeral realms and their implication is source for vast amounts of advetures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7557-profeta-del-pesar","name":"Profeta del Pesar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7557_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T13:51:24-07:00","id":658354,"title":"","content":"As a side question, how useful is Umbra (Revised) for gamelines other than Werewolf? Does it detail the Underworld (Dark Umbra)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1119-primal-flame","name":"Primal Flame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1119_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T17:40:00-07:00","id":658683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primal Flame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/601016-on-demon-the-fallen-and-the-umbra?p=658354#post658354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a side question, how useful is Umbra (Revised) for gamelines other than Werewolf? Does it detail the Underworld (Dark Umbra)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Umbra Revised is strictly about Werewolf's stomping grounds, so it doesn't cover the Dark Umbra, counts the High Umbra as part of the Deep Umbra, and is at direct odds with Mage due to not placing outer space as an interpretation of the spirit world (the Aetherial Realm is the Umbra corresponding to the physical outer space in Werewolf).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}